# Mac App Store apps — installed interactively by setup.sh.
#
# Kept separate from the main Brewfile on purpose: App Store apps are
# root-owned and `mas` must authorize through the App Store, so installing or
# upgrading them prompts for a password / Apple ID and cannot run unattended.
# setup.sh runs this once at bootstrap; routine `brew bundle` against the main
# Brewfile stays non-interactive and never touches these. Requires being signed
# into the App Store GUI first (Apple removed CLI sign-in). Regenerated by the
# update_brewfile() shell function. See CLAUDE.md.
